#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# fold_while_list

#% text
# `fold_while_list(f, x, xs, test)` gives the list of values `fold_while(f, x, xs, test)` goes through: `x`, then each new value, up to the first for which `test` is not `true`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
fold_while_list((a, b) => a/b, 120, range(10), is_integer)
#% output
#= [120, 120, 60, 20, 5, 1, 1/6]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# `fold_while_list(f, test)(x, xs)` is the operator form; with one argument the first element of `xs` is the start value.

#% cell
fold_while_list(subtract, is_positive)(12, [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6])
#% output
#= [12, 11, 9, 6, 2, -3]

#% cell
fold_while_list(add, less_than(20))(range(10))
#% output
#= [1, 3, 6, 10, 15, 21]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `fold_while`, `fold_list`
